WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:04.038
Lab 1 runs in the
non-person identity folder,

3
00:00:04.038 --> 00:00:07.300
in PowerShell 7, against
a fictional tenant.

4
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:12.200
Step one sends Microsoft's samples to
the fakes, and seventeen tests pass.

5
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.274
One of them is the whole risk in a
single test: it creates a credential

6
00:00:16.274 --> 00:00:20.275
from the Graph sample, then exchanges
a token with another subject.

7
00:00:20.275 --> 00:00:22.027
The create succeeds,

8
00:00:22.027 --> 00:00:26.975
and the exchange fails with A A
D S T S seven double oh two one.

9
00:00:26.975 --> 00:00:29.450
Step two lists what each task needs.

10
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:33.375
The read task holds two Graph
read permissions and Reader.

11
00:00:33.375 --> 00:00:38.537
Only the apply task holds application
read-write and Managed Identity Contributor.

12
00:00:38.537 --> 00:00:42.593
Step three builds the plan:
eight conversions in two waves,

13
00:00:42.593 --> 00:00:45.550
four exchange tests passed and two failed,

14
00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:50.450
seven findings and one warning, and
twenty actions, four of them writes.

15
00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:55.700
Nothing is sent, and the plan's hash is
the same on every run with these inputs.
